{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/205712-turn-blade-vs-just-bruised","id":205712,"title":"Turn blade Vs. Just Bruised","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-22T22:29:11-07:00","id":205712,"title":"Turn blade Vs. Just Bruised","content":"Need some input from people with a better grasp of the game system...<br /> <br /> Demons have two major Embeds for not dying: Turn Blade vs. Just Bruised. Can someone lay out the benefits of each, especially as compared to the other? Would there be an incentive to take both?<br /> <br /> And can someone verify the experience I've had that demons are not as good as some other splats (Werewolves, Vampires, Prometheans) at handling damage?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T23:05:07-07:00","id":205762,"title":"","content":"Just Bruised: Works on most sources of damage, use is declared after incident occurs; effectiveness degrades over multiple uses, does nothing to reduce damage type.<br /> Turn Blade: Consistent dicepool, can reduce damage type; can do nothing to mitigate damage quantity stemming from pure attack successes, only works on attacks the demon is aware of.<br /> <br /> Also the former is affinity for Destroyers and the latter is affinity for Guardians, which could probably be discerned from the above comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}